
# ---- subject line ------------------------------------------------------
# Write it on the blank first line, as:
#
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
#   type     feat | fix | refactor | perf | style | docs | test | build |
#            ci | chore | revert          (chore is the catch-all)
#   scope    optional; the sub-project or area touched, e.g. include, cmd,
#            tests, py, c, rust, csharp, wasm, benches, fuzzing, scripts,
#            docsgen, ci
#   subject  lowercase, imperative mood, no trailing period, <= 72 columns
#
# ---- body (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Wrap at 72 columns. Explain why the change is needed; the diff already
# shows what changed.
#
# ---- footers (optional) ------------------------------------------------
#   Closes #123
#   Co-authored-by: <Model Name> <email>
#
# Add a Co-authored-by trailer only when a model actually produced the work
# being committed, and name the exact model. State the version when it is
# actually known, and omit it when it is not -- never guess one.
#
# Use one trailer per participating model, each with a
# @users.noreply.github.com address that is not tied to a real GitHub
# account:
#
#   Co-authored-by: DeepSeek V3.2 <deepseek@users.noreply.github.com>
#   Co-authored-by: GPT-5.6 <codex-gpt-5.6@users.noreply.github.com>
#
# See CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
# ---- full example ------------------------------------------------------
#
#   fix(rust): free strings through C API
#
#   The binding leaked the converted buffer whenever conversion returned an
#   error, because the error path skipped the deallocation helper.
#
#   Closes #399
#   Co-authored-by: DeepSeek V3.2 <deepseek@users.noreply.github.com>
#
# ---- enable this template ----------------------------------------------
#   git config commit.template .gitmessage
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
